# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your real values.
# .env.local is already excluded from Git — never commit real credentials.
#
# Both values below are found in your Supabase project dashboard under
# Project Settings -> API. They are the PUBLIC/publishable pair, safe to
# expose in browser code — never put a service_role / secret key here.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Milestone 8 — Payments, Invoicing and Receipts (Razorpay)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# All three values below come from the Razorpay Dashboard (use TEST MODE
# keys while developing — never live/production keys in a shared or
# non-production environment). Settings -> API Keys gives you Key ID/Key
# Secret; Settings -> Webhooks gives you the webhook secret once you create
# a webhook pointing at https://<your-domain>/api/webhooks/razorpay.
#
# RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET and RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET must NEVER be prefixed
# with NEXT_PUBLIC_ — doing so would ship them to the browser. Only
# RAZORPAY_KEY_ID is ever sent to the client (Razorpay's Checkout.js needs
# it to open the payment modal; it is not a secret).
#
# The app builds and runs fine with these unset — payment actions simply
# show a "Payment gateway is not configured" state instead of crashing. See
# docs/payments-billing-guide.md for the full setup walkthrough, including
# the one-time database bootstrap step (supabase/migrations/0005_payments_billing.sql's
# BOOTSTRAP section) that must ALSO be done — these env vars alone are not
# sufficient, since checkout/webhook verification reads the same two
# secrets from a database table, not from process.env, at verification time.
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Absolute base URL of this deployment (no trailing slash), e.g.
# https://app.nextwise.example — used to build the copyable "pay this
# invoice" links admins generate, and as the canonical site URL for page
# metadata (src/config/site.ts SITE_URL, Open Graph tags, etc.). Falls back
# to a relative path (still usable within the app) when unset. Defaulted to
# the standard local dev server URL below — change this to your real
# deployment URL in production.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Milestone 9 — Global University and Course Data Platform (CLI tools only)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These two values back the three `*-education-data` npm scripts
# (validate:education-data, import:education-data, seed:education-data —
# see docs/global-education-data-guide.md and scripts/*-education-data.ts).
# They are NEVER prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_. NEVER commit real values for
# either of these to source control.
#
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY: Settings -> API -> service_role secret in your
# Supabase project dashboard. Bypasses Row Level Security by design — used
# by scripts/import-education-data.ts (Milestone 9, run locally/CI, never
# in the browser) to write universities/courses rows directly, outside the
# Admin UI, AND (Milestone 10 — Electronic Signature Integration) by
# src/app/api/webhooks/signature/route.ts to upload a signed agreement
# document to Storage once a signature completes — see
# src/lib/supabase/service-role.ts for exactly why that one route needs
# it (it carries no admin session to write through, same reason its
# database writes use a SECURITY DEFINER function instead). Every OTHER
# read/write anywhere else in this application, in every milestone, still
# goes through the signed-in user's own RLS-scoped session
# (src/lib/supabase/server.ts) — this key is used in NO other file. If
# left unset, signature status still updates correctly; only the
# automatic signed-document capture step is skipped (see
# docs/milestones/M10-electronic-signature.md "What needs manual
# configuration").
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# SUPABASE_DB_URL: Database Settings -> Connection string -> URI in your
# Supabase project dashboard, with the database password filled in. Used
# only by scripts/seed-education-data.ts to apply
# supabase/seed/0003_global_education_dev_seed.sql via a raw Postgres
# connection.
SUPABASE_DB_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Milestone 10 — Electronic Signature Integration (F-122)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The app builds and runs fine with ALL FIVE of these unset — the
# signature provider defaults to a built-in, in-memory mock (see
# src/lib/signatures/mock-provider.ts) that needs no configuration at all,
# and in non-production environments a fixed development-only webhook
# secret is used automatically so the mock provider's full request ->
# webhook loop works out of the box (see src/lib/signatures/config.ts).
#
# SIGNATURE_PROVIDER: which SignatureProvider implementation to use (see
# src/lib/signatures/get-provider.ts). Defaults to 'mock'. This milestone
# ships no real provider integration — set this only once a real adapter
# (DocuSign/Dropbox Sign/Adobe Sign/Zoho Sign/etc.) has actually been
# added there; see docs/milestones/M10-electronic-signature.md "Future
# provider integration".
SIGNATURE_PROVIDER=

# SIGNATURE_API_KEY / SIGNATURE_API_SECRET: a real provider's own API
# credentials, read only by that provider's adapter once one exists (see
# SIGNATURE_PROVIDER above) — unused by the mock provider. Like
# RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET, SIGNATURE_API_SECRET must NEVER be prefixed with
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ — doing so would ship it to the browser.
SIGNATURE_API_KEY=
SIGNATURE_API_SECRET=

# SIGNATURE_WEBHOOK_SECRET: the HMAC secret src/app/api/webhooks/
# signature/route.ts and public.apply_signature_webhook_event()
# (0011_electronic_signature.sql) both verify incoming webhook deliveries
# against. Must NEVER be prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_. Choose a long random
# string. This env var alone is NOT sufficient in production — webhook
# verification also reads an independent copy of the same value from a
# database table (signature_provider_config), same "two independent
# copies" pattern RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET already established for
# payment_gateway_config; see that migration's BOOTSTRAP section for the
# one-time SQL statement that must ALSO be run with the identical value.
SIGNATURE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# SIGNATURE_ENVIRONMENT: e.g. 'sandbox' or 'production' — purely
# descriptive, passed through to a real provider adapter once one exists;
# never interpreted by this application itself.
SIGNATURE_ENVIRONMENT=